### Sensor service - test requests (VS Code REST Client: click "Send Request" above each one)
### Run them in order. Identity (5101) and Sensor (5182) must both be running.

@sensor = http://localhost:5182
@identity = http://localhost:5101
@deviceId = TREEO_SIM_01
@deviceKey = sim-key-change-me-0123456789

### 0. Health check -> 200
GET {{sensor}}/health

### 1. Device sends a reading (what the ESP32 does every 5 s) -> 200 with pumpSeconds/autoWatering
POST {{sensor}}/api/sensors/readings
Content-Type: application/json
X-Device-Key: {{deviceKey}}

{ "deviceId": "{{deviceId}}", "moisture": 42, "pumpOn": false, "wifiRssi": -58, "firmware": "http-test" }

### 2. Same device with a WRONG key -> 401
POST {{sensor}}/api/sensors/readings
Content-Type: application/json
X-Device-Key: wrong-key-wrong-key-wrong

{ "deviceId": "{{deviceId}}", "moisture": 42, "pumpOn": false }

### 3. Log in as a user to get a token
# @name login
POST {{identity}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "champ@test.com", "password": "12345678" }

###
@token = {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### 4. Pair the device with this account -> 200
POST {{sensor}}/api/sensors/devices
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{ "deviceId": "{{deviceId}}", "deviceKey": "{{deviceKey}}", "name": "Money Tree" }

### 5. My devices (live moisture, online, pump) -> 200
GET {{sensor}}/api/sensors/devices
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 6. Water now for 5 seconds -> 202 (409 if the device has not reported in the last 30 s)
POST {{sensor}}/api/sensors/devices/{{deviceId}}/water
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{ "seconds": 5 }

### 7. Device's next reading picks up the command -> pumpSeconds = 5
POST {{sensor}}/api/sensors/readings
Content-Type: application/json
X-Device-Key: {{deviceKey}}

{ "deviceId": "{{deviceId}}", "moisture": 42, "pumpOn": false }

### 8. Pump on ... (opens a PumpRun)
POST {{sensor}}/api/sensors/readings
Content-Type: application/json
X-Device-Key: {{deviceKey}}

{ "deviceId": "{{deviceId}}", "moisture": 45, "pumpOn": true }

### 9. ... pump off (closes the PumpRun and sends a "pump" notification)
POST {{sensor}}/api/sensors/readings
Content-Type: application/json
X-Device-Key: {{deviceKey}}

{ "deviceId": "{{deviceId}}", "moisture": 63, "pumpOn": false }

### 10. 24-hour chart data -> 24 points + pump runs
GET {{sensor}}/api/sensors/devices/{{deviceId}}/history?hours=24
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 11. Recent pump runs
GET {{sensor}}/api/sensors/devices/{{deviceId}}/activity?limit=5
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 12. Turn auto-watering off (the device gets autoWatering=false in its next reply)
PATCH {{sensor}}/api/sensors/devices/{{deviceId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{ "autoWatering": false }

### ----- New rules (run 13 to 18 in order, within 30 s of each other so the device stays online) -----

### 13. Water now -> 202 "Watering command sent to the device."
POST {{sensor}}/api/sensors/devices/{{deviceId}}/water
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{ "seconds": 5 }

### 14. Press it again -> 202 "A watering command is already waiting for the device." (no second run queued)
POST {{sensor}}/api/sensors/devices/{{deviceId}}/water
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{ "seconds": 5 }

### 15. The pump is already running (automatic run) -> pumpSeconds = 0: the command is HELD, not lost
POST {{sensor}}/api/sensors/readings
Content-Type: application/json
X-Device-Key: {{deviceKey}}

{ "deviceId": "{{deviceId}}", "moisture": 28, "pumpOn": true }

### 16. Pump stopped -> pumpSeconds = 5: the held command is delivered now
POST {{sensor}}/api/sensors/readings
Content-Type: application/json
X-Device-Key: {{deviceKey}}

{ "deviceId": "{{deviceId}}", "moisture": 70, "pumpOn": false }

### 17. Soil is very wet (90 %)
POST {{sensor}}/api/sensors/readings
Content-Type: application/json
X-Device-Key: {{deviceKey}}

{ "deviceId": "{{deviceId}}", "moisture": 90, "pumpOn": false }

### 18. Water now on wet soil -> 409 "The soil is already wet (90%)..."
POST {{sensor}}/api/sensors/devices/{{deviceId}}/water
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{ "seconds": 5 }

### 19. Without a token -> 401
GET {{sensor}}/api/sensors/devices

### 20. Unpair (deletes this device's history) -> 204
DELETE {{sensor}}/api/sensors/devices/{{deviceId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
